Z||000000||86SE||03-11-2000||12:50 AM||||How much HP does a '86 2.8 Fiero engine put out at the wheels?  Is the rated 140 HP at the wheels or at the flywheel??<P>How about with wide open exhaust & high flow air filter how much HP can this engine produce??||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||03-11-2000||01:52 AM||||I believe GM began using net hp rather than gross hp back in the early 70's.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||03-11-2000||06:58 AM||||I'v seen dyno results that put the rear wheel hp at about 100-110||||reg||1
Z||000003||mwbackus||03-11-2000||12:27 PM||||  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/engdyn28.jpg">  <P>Image found on RS Motorsports website.  They use it as a comparison for their supercharger info.<P>Mike<p>[This message has been edited by mwbackus (edited 03-12-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||1FST2M6||03-11-2000||11:36 PM|||| <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/2m6dyno.jpg</A>    122.1HP and 159lbft.. at the wheels with 96,000 miles.||||reg||1
Z||000005||terryk||03-12-2000||02:32 AM||||Some site has a test of 4 85 V6 Fiero's. None would do better than 119 HP at the wheels. <P>With tons of bolt on, the best they got was 131 HP at the wheels. Not too shabby for a little 2.8L. I'll try to dig it up.||||reg||1
